8768	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-17T09:55:06.379Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S1 covers the upstream tracker capability checks, extraction and distinct missing-tool/sign-in errors.","evidence":"DEF S001 ac1–ac4 require successful capability-checked loading, refusal naming missing capabilities, GitHub parity and distinct tool/sign-in errors. HLD §5.1 assigns extraction and the timeout to s1. The proposed loader, adapter, runner and migration cover those responsibilities. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Retain this scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The two compatibility exceptions have upstream authorization to relax ac3 and k4.","evidence":"DEF still says results are 'the same as before' and a policy-free repo behaves 'exactly as it does today'. HLD requires a 10-second timeout, but the reviewed documents do not establish acceptance of both exceptions. This LLD itself lists acceptance as an open question. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Record explicit acceptance of the exceptions in the upstream contract before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Typed creation currently retries after every typed-attempt failure, and label lookup conflates failure with absence.","evidence":"ghCreateIssueTyped wraps both execution and parsing in an unconditional catch before the untyped POST: 'catch { /* org may not have issue types — fall through untyped */ }'. ghFindIssueByLabels uses 'catch { return undefined; }' and selects '.[0].number'. The shared execution helpers currently supply no timeout. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Preserve the stated baseline in regression tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The documented configuration precedence matches current valid configuration behavior.","evidence":"resolveGithubConfig checks the repo entry before default. resolveEntry receives allowEntryTarget=false for default, accepts an own owner/repo pair without type, and uses gitOriginOwnerRepo for explicit type github without a complete target. Explicit none disables integration. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts]","action":"Keep strict validation separate from this lenient resolver.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The port is new, while its detailed issue result and synchronous execution seam already exist with the stated shapes.","evidence":"Source searches found no existing TrackerPort or PortResult implementation. github.ts defines CreatedIssue with readonly ref:string, id:number and typed:boolean. TrackerExec accepts readonly argv and optional ExecFileSyncOptions; _setTrackerExecForTests replaces the shared executor. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Reuse or re-export CreatedIssue consistently rather than maintaining duplicate definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The migration inventory includes the production callers of the moved wrappers and preserves bugfix dependency signatures.","evidence":"Repository-wide searches locate these callers in tracker-auto.ts, bugfix/tracker.ts, questions.ts and setup.ts, plus listMyOpenTasks inside github.ts. Reading the implementations confirms readonly create labels, numeric childId, both optional factory options, and createBugfixTrackerIssue passing created.id to linkToParent. No additional production callers of queryTasks or ghCurrentLogin were found outside github.ts. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/bugfix/tracker.ts, src/workflow/questions.ts, src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Use this inventory for migration regression coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S1 can retain existing stored tracker records without a migration.","evidence":"TrackerMeta stores optional string references and reference maps. readTrackerMeta returns the existing nested block; patchTrackerMeta merges '{ adapter: \"github\", ...prior, ...patch }'. The proposed port retains string IssueRef and leaves these writers and fields unchanged. HLD assigns units and revision additions to s4. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Pin existing record contents in the proposed parity tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design preserves the HLD sc1 signatures and has a durable supersession record for the competing abstraction.","evidence":"HLD §4.1 has the same synchronous loader and seven port methods; issueOps is explicitly proposed as an addition. HLD assigns policy reading to s2 and orchestration/revisions to s4. The earlier LLD contains 'Superseded (2026-10-17)' and 'Do not build from this document', naming this s1 port as the sole abstraction. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, docs/standalone/add-add-items-tracker-setting-have-E2026100638436e90/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Carry the proposed issueOps amendment into the shared contract before dependent stories implement against it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Throwing on failed port results, with the three documented exceptions, preserves the inspected legacy caller failure behavior.","evidence":"linkToParent catches link errors and returns false; closeBugfixTrackerIssue closes before returning closed and has no close catch. Relink recovery records then closes, while undefined lookup returns 'relink-by-label found no matching issue'. Epic adoption occurs before its create catch. questions.ts catches comment failures. ghCreateLabel returns false on any error, and ghEnsureMilestone swallows creation errors. [files: src/workflow/bugfix/tracker.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/questions.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts]","action":"Keep unwrapping inside the existing catch boundaries, as designed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each S001 acceptance criterion has a proposed test mapping supported by the existing test seam.","evidence":"DEF S001 ac1–ac4 map respectively to loader success, capability refusal, operation/caller parity and tool/sign-in classification tests in §6. TrackerExec exposes execution options needed to inspect timeout settings. Existing tasks tests assert the empty-login error, and bugfix tests cover link failure, close propagation and relink recovery. These are planned tests, not verified implementation results. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tasks.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/bugfix-tracker.test.ts]","action":"Implement the mapped tests and run the affected suites; this review did not execute tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":10,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-17T09:55:06.379Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
